    "field": "Global carbon cycle",
    "problem": "The contribution of long-term, human-driven reductions in global wildfires to the enhancement of the terrestrial carbon sink is a poorly understood mechanism, often overshadowed by factors like CO2 fertilization.",
    "method": "Using the CLASS-CTEM modeling framework, we perform historical simulations driven by changes in population density and cropland area to quantify their effects on global burned area and wildfire CO\u2082 emissions, and to assess the resulting impact on the land carbon sink from 1850-2014.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify how the reduction in global burned area and wildfire emissions since the 1930s, driven by increasing population density and cropland expansion, has enhanced carbon uptake by the terrestrial biosphere.",
